   523	parent and the identity-verified manager-owned worker — are identical to v1.
   524	
   525	Second, the worker session admits a driver with no graph phase. One v2 session
   526	performs **at most one** read-only graph phase of at most one driver-defined
   527	command, waits while the parent validates the complete graph, accepts exactly
   528	one authenticated build permit, and performs exactly one compile phase of
   529	exactly one driver-defined command. v1 requires exactly one `go list` and
   530	exactly one `go build`; v2's "at most one" graph phase is a different session
   531	shape, which is a second independent reason the identity must differ. The v2
   532	session admits no retry, second graph phase, second compile phase, additional
   533	executable, shell, VCS operation, dependency download, generator, test, run, or
   534	tool request. A driver that cannot map its pipeline onto that session shape MUST
   535	NOT be admitted in this version; widening the session shape further requires yet
   536	another execution-policy identity, a new claim schema version, and its own
   537	review.
   538	
   539	Because both identities are closed constants inside the canonical build input, a
   540	v1 entry and a v2 entry can never alias in the cache, a receipt, a marker, or a
   541	claim, and a reader that knows only v1 cannot mistake a v2 artifact for a
   542	portable Go artifact.
   543	
   544	The per-operation host capability evidence record is re-versioned to
   545	`capability-evidence-v2`, reserved here and minted by the integration task, for
   546	two reasons that are both semantic rather than structural. `capability-evidence-v1`
   547	is normatively closed to `execution_policy: "manager-worker-v1"` — any other
   548	value is `build_execution_hardened_claim_forbidden` — so it cannot report a v2
   549	operation at all. And because section 9 admits a manifest mixing Go and
   550	additional-driver commands in one operation, one operation can be active under
   551	both identities, which v1's exactly-one-record-per-operation cardinality cannot
   552	express. `capability-evidence-v2` keeps the closed member set
   553	`{record_version, execution_policy, platform, controls}` and the probe-once-per-
   554	operation rule unchanged; it admits `execution_policy` drawn from exactly
   555	`{manager-worker-v1, manager-worker-v2}`, and the manager emits one record per
   556	distinct execution-policy identity active in the operation, all sharing that
   557	operation's single probe result and `probed_at`. Any other `execution_policy`
   558	value, including a hardened one, remains
   559	`build_execution_hardened_claim_forbidden`. The record stays result-only and
   560	MUST NOT enter a cache key, receipt input, marker record, or claim, so
   561	re-versioning it moves no frozen byte and `capability-evidence-v1` keeps its
   562	exact meaning for every v1-only operation.
   563	
