   568	`conformance/v1/vectors/go-host-execution-policy.json` and the "drifted
   569	capability-evidence record" release-gate case both name it. Both are correct at
   570	rc.5, where the version does not exist, and both stay frozen and correct for
   571	rc.5. When rc.6 mints the record, `TASK-260728-251p01` MUST move those two
   572	literals to a version that remains unminted and MUST NOT change the rc.5 corpus
   573	bytes or the rc.5 pin to do so. The boundary gate proves the current state
   574	positively rather than by absence: it requires the frozen corpus to keep
   575	rejecting the reserved version.
