   577	Before the compile phase, each driver MUST apply an exhaustive, deterministic,
   578	pre-compile rejection matrix computed from the validated snapshot and its graph
   579	phase, in the same position where `go-v1` rejects `SysoFiles`, native inputs,
   580	and the non-standard `//go:cgo_import_dynamic` directive. The matrix MUST reject
   581	every package-selected code-execution surface for that language, including build
   582	scripts, procedural and compiler macros, compiler and build-system plugins,
   583	annotation processors, source generators, manifest programs, build tasks and
   584	recipes, response files, package-selected linkers and native libraries, and
   585	network or registry access. A surface that cannot be rejected deterministically
   586	before the compile phase MUST cause the driver to be rejected, and MUST NOT be
   587	answered by a runtime allowance, an advisory warning, or a sandbox promise. The
   588	shared semantic class for such a rejection is
   589	`build_package_code_execution_forbidden`; each driver contract defines its own
   590	per-surface diagnostics beneath it.
   591	
   592	### 8. Cache, receipt, marker, and claim identity
   593	
   594	`curator-build-source-v1` is unchanged and is reused as the source identity for
   595	every driver in both source modes. It hashes bytes, not language, so no new
   690	                  "-module-name", <module>,
   691	                  "-no-color-diagnostics",
   692	                  <sources…>, "-o", <staged-artifact> ]
   693	graph_args   := [ "-###" ] ++ compile_args
   694	compile_argv := [ program ] ++ compile_args
   695	graph_argv   := [ program ] ++ graph_args
   696	```
   697	
   698	The relation is stated as a **construction** rather than as a comparison,
   699	because the cycle-1 wording — "they differ in exactly one token, at index 0" —
   700	is ambiguous when read as complete argv: index 0 is the *program*, and `-###` is
   701	an **insertion after** it. Mechanically, and all asserted rather than assumed:
   702	`len(graph_args) == len(compile_args) + 1`; `graph_args[0] == "-###"`;
   703	`graph_args[i+1] == compile_args[i]` byte-exactly for every `i`;
   704	`graph_argv[1] == "-###"`; `-###` occurs **exactly once** in `graph_argv` and
   705	**never** in `compile_argv`; and both vectors share one `program`.
   706	
   707	`-###` cannot collide with another token — sources are absolute paths and the
   708	module name matches `^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}$` — but the uniqueness is
   709	asserted anyway, because "cannot collide" is an argument and an assertion is a
   710	check.
   711	
   712	That is the property the graph phase rests on: the plan the manager verifies is
   713	the plan the compile phase executes, because both come from **one** builder and
   714	cannot drift. Five negatives are exercised — no insertion, doubled, appended
   715	instead of inserted, present in the compile vector, and a second token co-mutated
   716	under cover of the insertion — and all five must be rejected.
   717	
   718	**`graph_argv` is executed. `compile_argv` is not.** It is the compilation
   719	*request* the plan is derived from, and the object those seven properties are
   720	asserted over. What runs after the compile permit is the verified plan itself,
   721	job by job, under section 4 — so "the plan verified is the plan executed" stops
   722	being an inference about a deterministic planner and becomes a fact about which
   723	processes start. One graph phase and one compile phase are unchanged; the
   724	compile phase is now a bounded sequence of the plan's own jobs rather than a
   725	second `swiftc` invocation that re-plans out of sight.
   726	
   727	`<native-triple>` is the Stage A resolved `target.triple`, `<presented-sdk>` is
   728	the manager-owned presentation of section 4, `<module>` is the
   729	`curator-swift-module-v1` derivation of section 6 over the consuming command
   730	key, `<sources…>` is the ordered source set of section 6, and
   731	`<staged-artifact>` is inside operation-private manager staging. None is copied
   732	from a manifest, a descriptor, or an unvalidated package string.
